<% layout('layouts/main', {
	image: true,
}) %>

<main>
	<h1>The Team</h1>
	<div class="panel">
		<h2>David F. Chapman</h2>
		<img src="/img/david-f-chapman.jpg" alt="David F. Chapman">
		<p><strong>David F. Chapman</strong> is a writer, game designer, and developer, best known for creating the Vortex system that powers <em>Cubicle 7</em>’s <strong>Doctor Who: Roleplaying Game</strong>. He has worked on many RPG projects from a variety of publishers, including <strong>Buffy the Vampire Slayer</strong>, <strong>All Flesh Must Be Eaten</strong>, <strong>Terra Primate</strong>, <strong>Conspiracy X 2.0</strong>, <strong>Star Trek Adventures</strong>, <strong>Spirits of Manhattan</strong>, and more. He is currently line developer for the second edition of <strong>Doctor Who: The Roleplaying Game</strong> for <em>Cubicle 7</em>, and is also founder of the <strong>#RPGaDAY</strong> initiative, spreading positivity about tabletop gaming worldwide throughout August every year.</p>
	</div>
	<div class="panel">
		<h2>Stoo Goff</h2>
		<img src="/img/stoo-goff.jpg" alt="Stoo Goff">
		<p><strong>Stoo Goff</strong> is a programmer, game designer, musician and writer hailing from Norwich, now living in Glasgow. He is the designer and publisher behind the <strong>Aegean RPG</strong>, <strong>The Gaslight Club</strong> zine RPG, plus the writer and publisher of a number of supplements for a variety of RPGs. When not buried beneath a mountain of programming code or dreaming up new worlds and the rules which guide them, he is also the audio engineer behind the <strong>Tales from the Aletheian Society</strong> podcast.</p>
	</div>
</main>
